# Universal Cursor Rules

## UI/UX & Interaction Design
When generating, refactoring, or auditing UI/UX code, follow `skills/ui-ux-design/SKILL.md`:
- Feature-first layout; establish spacing & typography hierarchy in grayscale before color.
- Spacing scale: 4px, 8px, 12px, 16px, 24px, 32px, 48px, 64px.
- Line length (measure): 45-75 characters for readability.
- Touch targets: Minimum 44x44pt (iOS) or 48x48dp (Android/Web).
- Exactly one primary filled button per screen; secondary actions must be outlined or ghost.

## Backend & Architecture
When designing services, APIs, databases, or writing backend code, follow `skills/backend-architecture/SKILL.md`:
- The Dependency Rule: Dependencies point strictly inward. Domain entities and use cases must not depend on web or database frameworks.
- Functions must do one thing, stay under 20 lines, and maintain Command-Query Separation.
- Avoid nulls (use empty collections or Optionals). Throw domain exceptions over error codes.
- Use Outside-In TDD: write a Walking Skeleton before implementing feature logic.
